{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuE34JamMrVHC7LvgNgy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or wait for the rule to run, so I haven't checked that either works.\n\n**Fields:** the logs data view uses `timestamp` as its time field. The fields that matter for traffic are `response` (the status code, stored as a string), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `request`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-9fa32c2a Web logs overview\" (id `eff-9fa32c2a-web-logs-overview-4f9f270a4e1e`), with a default range of the last 7 days. It has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code (pie)\n- Average bytes by file extension\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-9fa32c2a 5xx spike\" (id `47ed393a-90a8-4b6e-b765-c1ff385a6354`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It checks every minute.\n- It fires when more than 10 documents with a `response` starting with 5 arrive in the last 5 minutes.\n- The tool creates rules disabled, so I enabled it.\n- I didn't attach any action, such as a notification, so a firing only shows up as an alert in Kibana."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":20383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1053},"output_tokens":452,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"ff57a5b8-b17c-4475-be3c-7314dc0adf96","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:57:19.035Z","request_id":"req_011CfuE343wvbdcoXeRTGKDK"}
